Subject: [flux] Allow "Flux" as a top-chrome WebUI name

WebUIContentsWrapperT static_asserts its page's name against an allowlist that
//chrome/browser/ui:webui_name_variants generates from this file. Hosting the
console anywhere in the browser frame instantiates that template, so without
the variant this is a compile error rather than a missing metric.

--- a/tools/metrics/histograms/metadata/page/histograms.xml
+++ b/tools/metrics/histograms/metadata/page/histograms.xml
@@ -635,6 +635,7 @@
   <variant name=".ExtensionsWebStoreZeroStatePromo"/>
   <variant name=".Feed"/>
   <variant name=".Feedback"/>
+  <variant name=".Flux"/>
   <variant name=".HistoryClustersSidePanel"/>
   <variant name=".HistorySidePanel"/>
   <variant name=".LensOverlayUntrusted"/>
